{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/tickets.py:11:config-class"], "search": "from pydantic import BaseModel", "replace": "from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict", "explanation": "Add the ConfigDict import needed for the v2 `model_config = ConfigDict(...)` form (migration.md#changes-to-config)."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/tickets.py:11:config-class"], "search": "    class Config:
        anystr_strip_whitespace = True", "replace": "    model_config = ConfigDict(str_strip_whitespace=True)", "explanation": "Pydantic V2 replaces the deprecated inner `class Config` with a `model_config` dict set via ConfigDict. Per the migration guide, `anystr_strip_whitespace` is renamed to `str_strip_whitespace`, and the value is unchanged."}], "notes": "Applied the config-class fix to Ticket: the inner `class Config` is replaced by `model_config = ConfigDict(str_strip_whitespace=True)`, and ConfigDict is imported. Pydantic-settings is not involved, and no other lines were touched.

Not changed, but needs review: `from_db_rows` passes integer primary keys (`r[0]`) into `ticket_id: str`. Pydantic V1 coerced ints to str. Pydantic V2 does not coerce int to str by default, so this will raise a ValidationError at runtime. The fix would be `coerce_numbers_to_str=True` in the ConfigDict, or converting with `str(r[0])` at the call site. I left this out because it is a behavior change beyond the listed finding and the instruction was to change only what the finding requires. Please decide which fix you want."}
